#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14622e0-0a8b-52f6-8bf8-44a04ea90e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437896} {:answer/id #uuid "422e0298-fb2d-5c6d-a4af-8cba072754ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b14622e0-0a8b-52f6-8bf8-44a04ea90e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437896} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddef766-7f45-5b44-b48d-737353d4be25" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522be474-9268-5719-9b67-fa3c52635318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437898} {:answer/id #uuid "37b81bb5-685b-583b-8db4-0245d173fc7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b81bb5-685b-583b-8db4-0245d173fc7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b79b55-bd9c-5274-8736-1fa18bb4e7d7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63da7652-c50c-579a-9313-44ed8eac188b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437900} {:answer/id #uuid "715c6b27-3b25-5248-a7ad-aceb0fe78ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63da7652-c50c-579a-9313-44ed8eac188b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437900} :answer-field/id #uuid "a893b756-f994-5e2f-ab56-a98d5a543109" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-131722" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system has no solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115241 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90d6f3fc-4b07-573d-909e-71ad76038bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113918} {:answer/id #uuid "95406019-b0d1-5bce-ac42-02cb3f8a5ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 - 3z \\\\ 2 + 3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113919} {:answer/id #uuid "db029453-b2ce-50e3-ba46-3321f56ef469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 3z \\\\ 2 + 3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113920} {:answer/id #uuid "e58beddf-d9e7-5f82-bbec-ff4bc4463d84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 - 3z \\\\ 2 - 3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113921} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd0d020-f064-5f3e-ada5-5a1b8e66bdc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 - 3z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113922}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6c202514-58b0-57fd-9d4a-d9d9f27c390e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113917}] :question/id #uuid "8cd9c6c5-780e-5f01-93cc-d5e9b9533129" :question/math-academy-id "q-42040" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n${x + 3z =-2; x + y = 0$.\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b9a3770-af37-58af-91e7-3430fd2463b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343154} {:answer/id #uuid "71cae964-c567-5585-ab23-7241fb114732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343221} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3da90-4b17-5b45-af78-2746f79a0b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343724} {:answer/id #uuid "ad97781e-f202-56a0-803a-f17ee1a49ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343764} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356} :answer-field/id #uuid "6517af05-6089-578f-972a-9310f8010c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0c28bd7-70de-59aa-93c9-933cbaca4593" :question/math-academy-id "q-74646" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=2 \\\\  & 2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ (k-7)y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$"}]}
